<div class="about-container">
	<title>10 Minute Files - About</title>
    <div class="section">
        <h1 class="title">Upload, Share, Self-destruct.</h1>
        <p class="description">
            10 Minute Files is a lightweight temporary file-hosting service. 
            Upload a file, get a short link, and share it instantly. Each link 
            lasts for 10 minutes, after which the file is permanently deleted. 
            It's a fast, disposable way to share files without leaving anything 
            behind.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h1 class="title">A Personal Note</h1>
        <p class="description">
            10 Minute Files isn't backed by a corporation or sponsor. It's just something I built
            because I miss the old version of the internet where simple tools existed just because someone
            thought they should. 10 Minute Files was built with no tracking, no dark patterns, no "growth strategy",
            and no way to monetize your usage. It's just a lightweight service that does one thing well and
            stays out of your way.
            <br><br>
            I run 10 Minute Files out of my own pocket because I believe the internet once thrived because of
            projects like this. If you find the service helpful or appreciate the philosophy behind it, there's
            a small <a href=/donate style="color:#fff">donation page</a> you can visit. Completely optional, but always appreciated.
            <br><br>
            - Vy
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="section" id="terms">
        <h2 class="title">Terms of Service</h2>
        <p class="description">By uploading a file to 10 Minute Files, you are agreeing to the following terms.</p>
        <p class="tos-content">Last update: June 21st, 2026</p><br>
        <div class="tos-section">
            <h3 class="tos-title">Information We Collect</h3>
            <p class="tos-content">
                10 Minute Files does not retain any files after their expiration period. 
                Once a file expires, it is securely erased and cannot be recovered.
                <br><br>
                For debugging, security, and service-quality purposes, we may 
                collect limited metadata about uploads, including but not limited to:
                <br> • File name
                <br> • IP addresses associated with the upload or download
                <br> • Ephemeral download key (e.g. <code style="font-family: monospace;">BGGJQHM5</code>)
                <br> • File extension & encoding
                <br> • File Size
                <br> • Number of times the file was downloaded
                <br>
                <br>No file contents are retained after expiration.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="tos-section">
            <h3 class="tos-title">File Storage & Retention</h3>
            <p class="tos-content">
                Uploaded files are stored temporarily and automatically deleted 10 
                minutes after upload. Once a file expires, it cannot be recovered or 
                re-downloaded. We do not keep backups or copies of expired files.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="tos-section">
            <h3 class="tos-title">Acceptable Use</h3>
            <p class="tos-content">
                You agree not to upload, share, or distribute any content that:
                <br> • Contains malware, viruses, or harmful code
                <br> • Infringes on copyrights or other intellectual property rights
                <br> • Is abusive, harassing, or intended to harm others
                <br> • Violates privacy rights, including doxxing or unauthorized personal data
                <br> • Is illegal under applicable laws
                <br> • Attempts to interfere with, disrupt, or overload the service
                <br> • Attempts to bypass file expiration or access controls
                <br>
                <br>We reserve the right to block users or remove content that violates these rules.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="tos-section">
            <h3 class="tos-title">Security Practices</h3>
            <p class="tos-content">
                10 Minute Files takes reasonable measures to secure uploaded files and associated metadata 
